<svelte:head><title>Docs · Kid StarterPack</title></svelte:head>
<main class="shell py-20 max-w-4xl"><span class="k-pill">DOCUMENTATION</span><h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-5">Get started in minutes.</h1><p class="text-slate-400 text-lg mt-5">Kid StarterPack lives in a single GitHub repository. Templates are standalone projects in subfolders; the website itself is generated from Markdown.</p>
<div class="mt-11 grid gap-5"><section class="glass p-7"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">01 · Pick a template</h2><p class="text-slate-400 mt-3">Start with a minimal welcome screen, an interactive app shell, a typed API or an authentication-ready fullstack starter.</p><a href={base + '/templates'} class="text-violet-300 inline-block mt-4">Explore templates →</a></section>
<section class="glass p-7"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">02 · Copy it with Giget</h2><p class="text-slate-400 mt-3">Run the command from a template detail page, replacing rifkinp after publication.</p><pre class="text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap break-all bg-[#0a0d17] border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 mt-4 text-violet-200">npx giget@latest gh:rifkinp/kid-starterpack/templates/frontend/sveltekit-minimal my-app</pre></section>
<section class="glass p-7"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">03 · Install and run</h2><pre class="text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap bg-[#0a0d17] border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 mt-4 text-violet-200">cd my-app
bun install
bun run dev</pre><p class="text-slate-400 mt-3">Fullstack starters additionally require .env credentials and database migrations; follow their README files.</p></section>
<section class="glass p-7"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">04 · Contribute</h2><p class="text-slate-400 mt-3">Add a self-contained folder under templates and a matching Markdown descriptor in content. GitHub Actions validates that paths and metadata agree.</p><p class="text-slate-400 mt-3">The repository's license is MIT; review third-party dependencies and use secure production configuration.</p></section></div></main>
